Cell["\<\
Note that dominance order is always sign reversed under transposition of \
partitions.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
The dominance order induces a lattice structure in the Young subgroups of the \
symmetric group. This plays a fundamental role in the representation theory \
of the symmetric group.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "3) Lexicographic order. This is a total order (zero is returned only for \
coinciding partitions). It coindices with (0-right-padded) lexicographic \
order of lists in ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Text"],

