Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
5.3. Words and the plactic monoid\
\>", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["\<\
A word is just a list of labels, and they can be repeated. We will later see \
a generalization to \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]double words\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] (my name) in which we have a list with two lists { \
slots, labels }. A word of length n is equivalent to the double word { \
Range[n], word }, but in the double word the slots (which must be integers \
1...m) can also be repeated.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
Given any semistandard tableau or skew-tableau, we associate to it a word in \
the following way:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"WordOfTableau", "[", "tab_Tableau", "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"DeleteCases", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Join", "@@", 
     RowBox[{"Reverse", "[", "tab", "]"}]}], ",", "Skew"}], "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
The process is obviously reversible for words constructed from a non-skew \
semistandard tableau, but not every word comes from such a tableau in this \
way, and the Skew information is lost in the conversion to a word, so many \
different skew-tableaux may give the same word. In fact every word comes from \
some (generally many) skew-tableau.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
We proceed in a different way: Given a word, there is a unique semistandard \
tableau whose word is Knuth-equivalent (see below) to the original word:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"TableauOfWord", "[", "word_List", "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"Fold", "[", 
   RowBox[{"RowBump", ",", 
    RowBox[{"Tableau", "[", "]"}], ",", "word"}], "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableauOfWord", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"a", ",", "b", ",", "c", ",", "a", ",", "d", ",", "c"}], "}"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 InterpretationBox[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    StyleBox[
     TagBox[GridBox[{
        {
         ItemBox["a",
          Frame->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
          StripOnInput->False], 
         ItemBox["a",
          Frame->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
          StripOnInput->False], 
         ItemBox["c",
          Frame->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
          StripOnInput->False], 
         ItemBox["c",
          Frame->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
          StripOnInput->False]},
        {
         ItemBox["b",
          Frame->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
          StripOnInput->False], 
         ItemBox["d",
          Frame->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
          StripOnInput->False], "", ""}
       },
       AutoDelete->False,
       GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
      "Grid"],
     StripOnInput->False,
     FontSize->10], TextForm]], "InlineText"],
  Text[
   Style[
    Grid[{{
       Item[Tableaux`Private`a, Frame -> RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
       Item[Tableaux`Private`a, Frame -> RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
       Item[Tableaux`Private`c, Frame -> RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
       Item[Tableaux`Private`c, Frame -> RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]}, {
       Item[Tableaux`Private`b, Frame -> RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
       Item[Tableaux`Private`d, Frame -> RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]}}], FontSize -> 
    10]]]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

