Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
5.5. Weight of a tableau. Kostka numbers\
\>", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["\<\
1) The weight of a tableau in a set S of labels is a list of integers \
counting how many times each label appears in the tableau, respectively. \
Hence weights are lists of integers, not necessarily partitions, though \
clearly the sum of the integers is the number of boxes. These lists are \
sometimes called \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]weak decompositions\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] of an integer.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "TableauWeight"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 StyleBox["\<\"TableauWeight[tab, set] returns the weight of the tableau \
w.r.t. the given set of labels. This is a list of the respective numbers of \
occurrences of the elements of set in the tableau tab. TableauWeight[tab] \
returns the weight in the set of the union of all entries, sorted.\"\>", 
  "MSG"]], "Print", "PrintUsage",
 CellTags->"Info3579442450-9818602"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"TableauWeight", "[", "tab_Tableau", "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"TableauWeight", "[", 
    RowBox[{"tab", ",", 
     RowBox[{"DeleteCases", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Union", "@@", "tab"}], ",", "Skew"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"TableauWeight", "[", 
    RowBox[{"tab_Tableau", ",", "labels_List"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"word", "=", 
       RowBox[{"WordOfTableau", "[", "tab", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Count", "[", 
        RowBox[{"word", ",", "#"}], "]"}], "&"}], "/@", "labels"}]}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}]}], "Input"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableauWeight", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Tableau", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "2", ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", "2", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"3", ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "3", ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"2", ",", "4", ",", "2", ",", "1"}], "}"}]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "2) Given a set S of labels, for any partition \[Lambda] and any weight \
\[Mu] we define the Kostka number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["K", "\[Lambda]\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " as the number of semistandard tableaux of partition \[Lambda] and weight \
\[Mu]. Sometimes the name Kostka number is restricted to the case in which \
\[Mu] is also a partition."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "3) A known result is that for a given partition there is always a single \
semistandard tableau with weight equal to the partition (this is called the \
Yamanouchi tableau of that partition, and has a very simple structure: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "i"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " copies of the i-th label in the i-th row):"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"tabs", "=", 
  RowBox[{"SemistandardTableaux", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "2", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"a", ",", "b", ",", "c"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   InterpretationBox[Cell[BoxData[
     FormBox[
      StyleBox[
       TagBox[GridBox[{
          {
           ItemBox["a",
            Frame->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
            StripOnInput->False], 
           ItemBox["a",
            Frame->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
            StripOnInput->False], 
           ItemBox["a",
            Frame->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
            StripOnInput->False]},
          {
           ItemBox["b",
            Frame->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
            StripOnInput->False], 
           ItemBox["b",
            Frame->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
            StripOnInput->False], ""},
          {
           ItemBox["c",
            Frame->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
            StripOnInput->False], "", ""}
         },
         AutoDelete->False,
         GridBoxItemSize->{
          "Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
        "Grid"],
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontSize->10], TextForm]], "InlineText"],
    Text[
     Style[
      Grid[{{
         Item[Tableaux`Private`a, Frame -> RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
