Cell[TextData[{
 "2) Take now partitions \[Lambda] and \[Mu], with respectively n and m \
boxes. Take also any partition \[Nu] with r=n+m boxes, and such that \[Nu] \
contains \[Lambda]. Fix a set of labels and work always with semistandard \
tableaux and semistandard skew-tableaux.\n\nThe question is: given a tableau \
V of shape \[Nu], in how many ways can we write it as a Schensted-product of \
two tableaux T and U or respective shapes \[Lambda] and \[Mu]? It is also the \
number of skew-tableaux {{Skew, U}, {T}} that rectify to V, and the number of \
skew tableaux of shape \[Nu]/\[Lambda] whose rectification is a given tableau \
of shape \[Mu].\n\nFor any tableau ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["U", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " with shape \[Mu] define\n\n\t\[ScriptCapitalS]( \[Nu]/\[Lambda], ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["U", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 ") = { skew-tableaux S on \[Nu]/\[Lambda] whose rectification is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["U", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 "}\n\nFor any tableau ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["V", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " with shape \[Nu] define\n\n\t\[ScriptCapitalT](\[Lambda], \[Mu], ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["V", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 ") = { {T,U} where T is a tableau on \[Lambda], U is a tableau on \[Mu] and \
T.U = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["V", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 "}\n\nFor any tableaux ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["U", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " on \[Mu] and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["V", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " on \[Nu] there is a canonical one-to-one correspondence between \
\[ScriptCapitalT](\[Lambda], \[Mu], ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["V", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 ") and \[ScriptCapitalS](\[Nu]/\[Lambda], ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["U", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 "). Hence the cardinalities of both sets are actually independent of the \
choice of the tableaux ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["U", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["V", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " and depend only on the partitions \[Lambda], \[Mu], \[Nu]. That \
cardinality is called a Littlewood-Richardson number, and it is denoted by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     SubscriptBox["c", "\[Lambda]"], "\[Nu]"], "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]]],
 ". Two important properties are\n\n\tSymmetry:   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     SubscriptBox["c", "\[Mu]"], "\[Nu]"], "\[Lambda]"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     SubscriptBox["c", "\[Lambda]"], "\[Nu]"], "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\tInvariance under transposition of the three partitions:   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     SubscriptBox["c", "\[Mu]"], "\[Nu]"], "\[Lambda]"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     SubscriptBox["c", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[Mu]", "t"]], 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Nu]", "t"]], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "t"]], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\nThis number is zero unless |\[Nu]| = |\[Mu]| + |\[Lambda]| and \[Nu] \
contains both \[Mu] and \[Lambda].\n\nThese numbers are relations among \
partitions, not among tableaux. We will use later tableaux to compute them, \
but always assuming that the set of labels is large enough so that there are \
no cancellations due to \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]dimensional\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] issues."
}], "Text"],

Cell["\<\
3) Define the Littlewood-Richardson skew tableaux:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"LRSkewTableauQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"tab_", ",", "labels_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"ReverseLatticeWordQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"WordOfTableau", "[", "tab", "]"}], ",", "labels"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input"],

Cell["Example in page 64 of Fulton:", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
   RowBox[{"all15", "=", 
    RowBox[{"SemistandardSkewTableaux", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"5", ",", "4", ",", "3", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"3", ",", "3", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "3", ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "//",
   "Timing"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
  "22.7894910000000017191723600262776017189`7.378334538663602", ",", "1300"}],
   "}"}]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

